CM 7-el Yagi @255 MHz (geometry-optimized for lowest SWR, NO matching network)
CM This version adjusts reflector/driven/director-1 lengths & spacing
CM to raise feed impedance toward ~40–45 ohms and reduce SWR.
CM forw: 90, 0 ; back: 90, 180
CE

SY rw=0.01
SY seg=41
SY freq=255

' --- Updated lengths (rebalanced for higher Zin) ---
SY Lr=0.572365' shorter reflector increases feed R
SY Ld=0.564138' longer driven raises impedance
SY L1=0.512312' slightly longer director1 shifts coupling
SY L2=0.512153
SY L3=0.497911
SY L4=0.481967
SY L5=0.480575

' --- half lengths ---
SY hr=Lr/2
SY hd=Ld/2
SY h1=L1/2
SY h2=L2/2
SY h3=L3/2
SY h4=L4/2
SY h5=L5/2

' --- Updated spacings to lift R-in ---
SY xr=-0.17992' reflector moved closer for higher R
SY xd=0.000
SY x1=0.199612' director1 moved further to reduce loading (raises R)
SY x2=0.420032
SY x3=0.713208
SY x4=1.062444
SY x5=1.436815

' ------- GEOMETRY --------
GW 1 41  xr 0 -hr   xr 0 hr  rw
GW 2 41  xd 0 -hd   xd 0 hd  rw
GW 3 41  x1 0 -h1   x1 0 h1  rw
GW 4 41  x2 0 -h2   x2 0 h2  rw
GW 5 41  x3 0 -h3   x3 0 h3  rw
GW 6 41  x4 0 -h4   x4 0 h4  rw
GW 7 41  x5 0 -h5   x5 0 h5  rw

GE 0
GN -1

' feed
EX 0 2 21 0 1 0

FR,0,1,0,0,255
PQ -1
PT -1
RP,0,37,73,1003,-180,0,5,5
